From 06fa1823029685fabb8341fe5928ef655be17279 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:12:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Rank plustek8200i above genesys

The 8200i SE (07b3:1825) is found by both genesys and plustek8200i, and
both ranked default_rank, so the order of the drivers decided and genesys
won. Genesys does not report its buttons, and opening the scanner through
it left the scanner without button events until it was power cycled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 data/scanner-devices.json | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/data/scanner-devices.json b/data/scanner-devices.json
index c4ecb8f..11ebbda 100644
--- a/data/scanner-devices.json
+++ b/data/scanner-devices.json
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
       "_comment": "For a scanner that more than one driver found: the lower the better. Drivers that speak a standard protocol work on more scanners than the vendor's. A driver not named here ranks default_rank, and one that goes through another host comes last.",
       "airscan": 0,
       "escl": 1,
+      "plustek8200i": 1,
       "hpaio": 8,
       "net": 9
   },
-- 
2.56.0

